lapse of panic disorder in adult outpatient responders to venlafaxine XR</article-title><year>2005</year><conf-name>Presented at Anxiety Disorders Association of America (ADAA)</conf-name><conf-date>March 17&#x02013;21</conf-date><conf-loc>Seattle, Washington</conf-loc></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Prien</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jarrett</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Conceptualization and rationale for consensus definitions of terms in major depressive disorder. Remission, recovery, relapse, and recurrence</article-title><source>Arch Gen Psychiatry</source><year>1991</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>851</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1929776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gelenberg</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lydiard</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudolph</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Efficacy of venlafaxine extended-release capsules in nondepressed outpatients with generalized anxiety disorder: A 6-month randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2000</year><volume>283</volume><fpage>3082</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10865302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gitlin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Venlafaxine, monoamine oxidase inhibitors, and the serotonin syndrome</article-title><source>J Clin Psychopharmacol</source><year>1997</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>66</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9004070</pub-